  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NCA-Coffee making skill for everyone</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Our initiative started when we first provided food consultancy classes in 2016. We offered opportunity for students who needed extra income to work with us as a part time kitchen hands, barista and waiter / waitress. That&#x2019;s when we built up our expertisein training and coaching skills. We are happy to see our students grow and get good occupation in various restaurants, hotel and caf&#xe9;. The Slurp Latte Art Smackdown in 2021 and 2022 is our signature initiative in promoting the art of coffee and empoweringpeople working in this sector, many of whom are women, many are from provinces and ethnic minority groups and some LGBTI.
In summary we provide:
&#x2022; Accessibility, inclusiveness and equity
&#x2022; Employability and productivity
&#x2022; Economic and social stabilityby reducing unemployment and creating skills.
Skillbender studio will aim to create Online masterclasses for those who are new to hospitality, food and beverages business as well as those already operating restaurants, caf&#xe9;, food stalls and sector investors. The intention for developing this platform is to help those who are not able to travel, who live in provinces, and young and senior who lack confidence.
Through our ongoing initiative we observed people have limited access to an existing TVET (Technique and Vocational Education and Training) colleges and businesses found it hard to get skilled staff. Yet many young people who dropout from school and new graduates who could not enter university or TVET are unemployed. There is also a mismatch betweenwhat students learn in school or institutions and labour market. Therefore, our initiative will provide another option in skill development through low cost and accessible learning opportunityfor future occupation or employment. Our program will alsobenefit seniors and people who have limited ability/resources to travel and communicate.
We hope this will help our students to have access to productive employment and income generation.
COVID 19 negatively impacted on peoples&#x2019; livelihood, compounded bycurrent economic downfall continues to make people&#x2019;s mobility more difficult and costly. At the same time opportunities for people to find employment is increasingly challenging.
Through various discussions with senior alumni, businesses and social enterprises I&#x2019;ve identified the gap between formal and informal learning opportunities and thoughtOnline platform might provide a useful approach in providing basic and advance classes in hospitality to prepare students to accessproductive employment or buildtheir own business tailored to their locality and communities&#x2019; needs.
As most people now have access to affordable mobile phones I thought our classes will not only provide knowledge in food and beverages area, but will also indirectly enhance participants&#x2019;knowledge in use of mobile tools and applications.
(FYI, this is extracted from first application, the complete description will be replaced later)</narrative>
  </description>
